From 55b766059aff6c88c4ab71a7df7f8ff7aed4ae9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:14:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08070/11362] [outer-loop] add sc25 + tn36 GameAdapters and fix
 the ka59 action-label parser

Three of the 25 public games could not build an offline induction window, so they
were silently absent from every A/B corpus built through build_progress_window:

  ka59  ValueError: invalid literal for int(): 'C:1'   -- unhandled click label
  sc25  AttributeError: 'NoneType'.hand_verifier       -- no adapter registered
  tn36  same                                            -- no adapter registered

I first reported these as three reverse-engineering projects. That was wrong, and
the registry is why: the RE was already done and captured. tn36 has a 340-line
general solver (scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py) plus a win_condition with
source line refs and the full program-editor mechanic; sc25 has
SC25_PLANS_BY_LEVEL[1..5] and apply_sc25_label. Building the adapters was
transcribing captured knowledge into the interface, not rediscovering mechanics.
The registry-first check is exactly what the check-registry-before-rederiving
rule exists for, and I skipped it.

ka59: GameAdapter gains an optional `label_to_action_data` hook, ka59 supplies
exp4340's canonical parser ("C:<i>" -> action 6 + {x,y}), and build_window uses
it. build_window now FAILS LOUD on an unparseable label rather than defaulting to
action 0 -- a Transition is the induction evidence the LLM reads, so a wrong
action would not crash, it would quietly teach false dynamics.

sc25: replays the banked L1 plan while at level 0 (the _ka59 pattern), then hands
back the real action space.

tn36: deliberately NOT a replayed list. The registry's own note says the slot
layout re-lays-out per level -- "DISCOVER, don't hardcode" -- and the solver
re-issues a click while an animation flag is set, so a fixed sequence would
desynchronise. The adapter is state-driven: it compares the live program to the
computed target and emits the next single bit-toggle still needed, then run. An
unregistered click leaves state unchanged and is re-emitted, matching the
solver's own retry convergence.

Also hoists `_default_json_apply` to module level; sp80 and others had it inline.

Verified: both new adapters reach L1 offline and build windows with a real
level-up transition (sc25 12/16, tn36 7/7). Corpus ceiling 20 -> 23. wa30 remains
unreachable and its missing reproduction path is filed in known-issues.
